What are Concurrent Collections?

Concurrent collections allow multiple threads to read and write shared data at the same time.

Traditional synchronized collections lock the entire data structure for every operation, causing thread contention.

Concurrent collections use fine-grained locking or lock-free atomic operations to let multiple threads work 
simultaneously.
They prevent runtime errors like ConcurrentModificationException by using weakly consistent or fail-safe iterators.






